<title>BRAZIL: Ford invests $170 mln to make Kas in Brazil.</title>
<headline>Ford invests $170 mln to make Kas in Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian subisdiary of Ford Motor Co said it would invest $170 million to produce the company's Ka cars in a factory in Brazil.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1997, Ford aims to produce 53,000 units of the Ford Ka,&quot; Ford Brasil said in a statement after senior company officials met with President Fernando Henrique Cardoso.</p>
<p>The investment is part of Ford's program to invest $2.5 billion in Brazil by 1999, the statement said.</p>
